    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# dsh-plans\n\nHuman-in-the-loop planning preset for the [DeepSeek Harness] (DSH): researched, refined Markdown plans before any code changes, then goal-driven execution after an explicit handoff.\n\nTurn a rough repository-change request into a traceable plan under `./dsh-plans/`, refine that plan with reviewer or criticizer subagent rounds, and hand the accepted plan to a persistent DSH goal that drives implementation until the plan's Verifier Checklist passes. Everything runs on DSH's native mechanisms — `ask_user_question`, subagents, the goal loop, and bundled skills — with no separate execution engine.\n\n## How a run goes\n\n1. The agent inspects the target repository read-only, then asks the workspace's language setting once (persisted for every later run in that workspace).\n2. Planning questions come one at a time, in a standard choice format (recommended option first, `Other` second-last, `Auto-complete` last); every question and answer is recorded in `DECISIONS.md` and the run ledgers.\n3. A mandatory final scope confirmation gates the first draft: `dsh-plans/YYYY-MM-DD-topic/PLAN_v1.md`, with stable IDs, evidence, and a `## Verifier Checklist`.\n4. After every plan version, a refinement mode question — a reviewer or criticizer never runs without the user (or `Auto-complete`) selecting it. Reviewer and criticizer subagents run through the preset's own `run_plan_subagent` tool: read-only by construction, with the model chosen for that role at its first use.\n5. After refinement converges, an explicit execution handoff question with no auto-complete: execute the plan now as a DSH goal, or stop after planning.\n6. On approval, execution runs as a DSH goal whose objective points at the accepted plan and its Verifier Checklist. Implementation follows `ponytail` simplification discipline and the MVP minimum-test set, and `update_goal` complete is called only when every checklist box passes.\n\n## Bundled skills\n\nFive skills, chosen by the agent for each request:\n\n| Skill | Use it when |\n|---|---|\n| `create-a-small-plan` | A small scoped repo change needs 1 to 3 planning questions. Recommended refinement: one criticizer round, then accept for execution. |\n| `create-a-plan` | A broad or risky change needs 5 to 10 planning questions and web research. Recommended refinement: one reviewer round, then one criticizer round, then accept for execution. |\n| `create-a-big-plan` | An open-ended or high-risk effort needs 10 or more planning questions and web research. Recommended refinement: one round of three concurrent reviewers consolidated by the main agent, then one criticizer round, then accept for execution. |\n| `diagnose-before-plan` | A bug, CI failure, regression, incident, RCA, or broken behavior needs diagnosis before planning. |\n| `reference-before-plan` | Downloaded projects, articles, papers, or docs must be analyzed before planning choices are safe. |\n\nWorkflow guarantees:\n\n- Per workspace, the language setting is asked once before the first planning question, and persisted.\n- Per role, the model for reviewer / criticizer / executor is asked once, at that role's first actual use, and persisted. Reviewer and criticizer children run through the preset's own `run_plan_subagent` tool (runtime model selection; write tools, goal tools, user questions, and delegation tools are denied to the child). The executor is the current session's goal loop, so its confirmed model is the session model.\n- One planning question at a time; the final scope confirmation gates `PLAN_v1.md`.\n- After every plan version, a refinement mode question — a reviewer or criticizer never runs without it.\n- After refinement, an explicit execution handoff question with no auto-complete: execute the plan now as a DSH goal, or stop after planning.\n- Execution runs as a DSH goal with `ponytail` simplification discipline and the MVP minimum-test set, so token cost stays proportional to the work.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.dsh/.agent-presets\ngit clone https://github.com/Optim-Agent/dsh-plans.git ~/.dsh/.agent-presets/dsh-plans\n```\n\nThe roster re-scans its roots on every read, so the new preset appears in the preset picker immediately — select `dsh-plans` for a new session (no restart needed). Then from any directory ask:\n\n```text\nCreate a plan for <your change>\n```\n\nUpdate an existing install with `git -C ~/.dsh/.agent-presets/dsh-plans pull`.\n\n## Code Mode requirement\n\n`dsh-plans` presents all tools through DSH Code Mode (`run_code` plus the generated TypeScript SDK). This avoids native function-schema incompatibilities in models that populate every optional Bash argument, while leaving the original Bash implementation, sandbox escalation checks, approvals, background jobs, and cancellation behavior unchanged.\n\nThe host must provide `codeRuntime`; the DSH Web profile already loads `dsh-code-runtime-worker-thread`. Profiles without a code runtime fail clearly while mounting the preset instead of falling back to the incompatible Native tool presentation. Presentation is fixed when an agent is composed, so open a new `dsh-plans` session after updating. Restarting the whole DSH service is not normally required, and existing sessions are not hot-migrated.\n\n## Runtime layout\n\nPublic artifacts stay in the workspace, ready to commit:\n\n```text\ndsh-plans/YYYY-MM-DD-topic/\n  DECISIONS.md\n  PROBLEM_ANALYSIS.md     # diagnose-before-plan only\n  REF_ANALYSIS.md         # reference-before-plan only\n  PLAN_v1.md\n  PLAN_v1_reviewer_comments.md\n  PLAN_v2.md\n```\n\nMachine state stays private beside the artifacts, never committed:\n\n```text\ndsh-plans/.state/         # .gitignore contains \".state/\" (created by the helper)\n  config.json             # language + per-role model settings\n  active.json\n  runs/<run-id>/          # run.json, decisions.jsonl, subagents.jsonl, refs.jsonl\n```\n\nLarge downloaded references live outside the repository by default, under `~/.cache/dsh-plans/refs/`.\n\n## Preset layout\n\n```text\nagent.cordis.yml                  The composition: standard agent + dsh-plans rows\npreset.yml                        Display metadata\nlib/plan-subagents.js             Local host plugin: run_plan_subagent tool\nskills/                           The five bundled skills + shared references\nscripts/dsh_plans_state.py        State helper CLI (stdlib only)\n```\n\nThe composition registers its own `skills/` directory through the loader's `baseUrl`, so the preset is relocatable: clone it anywhere under a preset root and it still finds its skills and its local plugin.\n\n## Safety model\n\nThe supported boundary is planning discipline, durable state, and explicit handoff. Before the handoff, the workflow writes only `dsh-plans/.state/` and `dsh-plans/` artifacts — never target source, configs, or tests. Reviewer and criticizer subagents are read-only structurally (`run_plan_subagent` denies file-write, goal, user-question, and delegation tools) and report back through their final output. `Auto-complete` may answer planning and refinement questions; it never approves goal execution, installs, deploys, merges, pushes, credential use, or anything that changes external state.\n\n## Verify\n\n```bash\nnode --test scripts/test_plan_subagents.js\npython3 scripts/validate_preset.py\npython3 scripts/dsh_plans_state.py init --workdir /tmp/dsh-plans-smoke\n```\n\n## License\n\nMIT. See [`LICENSE`](LICENSE).\n\n[DeepSeek Harness]: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "agent.cordis.yml",
      "content": "# The `dsh-plans` agent preset: the standard coding agent, plus the\n# prime-plans-style planning workflow — researched, refined Markdown plans\n# under `dsh-plans/` with human-in-the-loop questions, reviewer/criticizer\n# subagent rounds, and goal-driven execution after an explicit handoff.\n#\n# Everything in `standard` is here. What changes:\n#   - the persona states the planning-first discipline;\n#   - the bundled `skills/` directory registers as a custom skill root (the\n#     `!!js` expression resolves `baseUrl`, which is this preset's own\n#     directory, so the root follows the preset wherever it is installed);\n#   - built-in plan mode is disabled: `dsh-plans` replaces it with artifact\n#     planning (`PLAN_vN.md` files) and its own handoff questions;\n#   - a small local host plugin (`./lib/plan-subagents.js`, resolved relative\n#     to this file) registers `run_plan_subagent`: a subagent tool with a\n#     runtime `model` parameter and structural read-only filters for the\n#     reviewer/criticizer roles.\n#\n# This file is an AGENT-PLANE composition mounted by the roster exactly like\n# `standard`. The plane and realm rules from that file apply unchanged.\n\n# ── identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# The preset's own persona, shadowing the deployment default for this agent.\n# `{{model}}` and `{{cwd}}` resolve from the agent's own route and workspace.\n- id: persona\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-persona'\n  config:\n    text: |-\n      You are a planning-first coding agent powered by the {{model}} model, running on the DeepSeek Harness. Your working directory is {{cwd}}.\n\n      This session is composed from the `dsh-plans` preset, which adapts the prime-plans workflow to the Harness: repository changes are researched, written as traceable Markdown plans under `dsh-plans/`, refined through reviewer/criticizer subagent rounds with the user in the loop, and only then implemented as a DSH goal.\n\n      When the user asks for a repository change (or a diagnosis/reference study before one), select the matching bundled skill from the skill catalog — create-a-small-plan, create-a-plan, create-a-big-plan, diagnose-before-plan, or reference-before-plan — load it with the `skill` tool, and follow it exactly, including its shared normative references. The workflow, not your judgment of convenience, decides the order of questions, artifacts, and handoffs.\n\n      Core discipline:\n      - Per workspace, confirm the language setting first; confirm each role's model at that role's first use. Reviewer and criticizer subagents run with the `run_plan_subagent` tool, passing the persisted model.\n      - Ask one user question at a time through ask_user_question, in the standard choice format; record every decision in `DECISIONS.md` and the run ledgers.\n      - Never spawn a reviewer or criticizer without the refinement mode question; after every PLAN version ask the refinement question, and after refinement converges ask the execution handoff question: execute the plan now as a DSH goal, or stop after planning.\n      - Before that handoff answer arrives, write only `dsh-plans/` state and artifacts — never target source, configs, or tests. `Auto-complete` never approves goal execution, installs, deploys, merges, pushes, or destructive cleanup.\n      - After approval, drive implementation with create_goal and the plan's Verifier Checklist, using todo_write, ponytail discipline, and the MVP minimum test set; call update_goal complete only when every checklist box passes.\n\n- id: agent-instructions\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-instructions'\n  config:\n    maxBytes: 65536\n\n# ── shell ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# `shell-env` stays in the HOST composition; both shell tools consume the host\n# registry from here. See `standard` for the full reasoning.\n- id: tool-bash\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-bash'\n  disabled: !!js process.platform === 'win32'\n\n- id: tool-pwsh\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-pwsh'\n  disabled: !!js process.platform !== 'win32'\n\n# ── filesystem ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n- id: tool-fs\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-fs'\n\n- id: tool-fs-search\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-fs-search'\n  config:\n    sampleOverCapGlobResults: false\n\n# ── background jobs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n- id: tool-jobs\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-jobs'\n\n# ── skills ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# The skill REGISTRY lives in the host composition and is layered per scope;\n# these rows register into THIS preset's layer, so they need no realm.\n# `customSkillDirs` points at this preset's bundled skills. `baseUrl` is the\n# preset's own directory inside the loader's `!!js` scope, so the root\n# resolves wherever the preset is installed.\n- id: skill-filesystem\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-filesystem'\n  config:\n    customSkillDirs:\n      - !!js \"process.getBuiltinModule('node:url').fileURLToPath(new URL('skills/', baseUrl))\"\n\n- id: tool-skill\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-skill'\n\n# ── goals ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Only the model-facing tool; the goal SERVICE and its session driver stay on\n# the host plane. dsh-plans drives the execution phase through this tool.\n- id: tool-goal\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-goal'\n\n# ── plan mode ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Built-in plan mode is DISABLED in this preset. Its single-plan,\n# write-forbidden loop conflicts with artifact planning: dsh-plans writes\n# `PLAN_vN.md` artifacts under `dsh-plans/` during the planning phase and\n# enforces its own handoff questions instead of exit_plan_mode.\n- id: planning\n  name: cordis:group\n  group: true\n  disabled: true\n  isolate:\n    planMode: true\n  config:\n    - id: plan-mode\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-plan-mode'\n\n# ── compaction ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Identical to `standard`: compaction and the result pruner share one\n# entry-local realm; the token meter stays on the host plane.\n- id: compaction\n  name: cordis:group\n  group: true\n  isolate:\n    compaction: true\n    toolResultPruner: true\n  config:\n    - id: compaction-basic\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-compaction-basic'\n\n    - id: command-compact\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-command-compact'\n\n    - id: tool-result-pruner\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-compaction-tool-result-pruner'\n      config:\n        thresholdChars: 8192\n        headChars: 4096\n        tailChars: 1024\n\n# ── delegation and workflows ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# The `subagents` registry and its spawn/fork backends live in the HOST\n# composition; this preset contributes the delegation TOOLS, which resolve\n# that host registry. `workflows` shares one entry-local realm (see\n# `standard` for why). Product provider rows stay disabled templates.\n- id: delegation\n  name: cordis:group\n  group: true\n  isolate:\n    workflowEngine: true\n  config:\n    - id: tool-subagent-control\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent-control'\n\n    - id: tool-subagent-list-agents\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent-control/list-agents'\n\n    - id: tool-subagent\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent'\n      config:\n        provider: spawn\n        toolName: subagent\n        backgroundMode: continuable\n\n    - id: tool-subagent-fork\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent'\n      config:\n        provider: fork\n        toolName: subagent_fork\n        backgroundMode: continuable\n\n    - id: tool-subagent-codex\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent'\n      disabled: true\n      config:\n        provider: codex\n        toolName: subagent_codex\n        enableRunInBackground: false\n        maxDepth: provider-managed\n\n    - id: tool-subagent-claude-code\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent'\n      disabled: true\n      config:\n        provider: claude-code\n        toolName: subagent_claude_code\n        enableRunInBackground: false\n        maxDepth: provider-managed\n\n    - id: workflow-worker-thread\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-workflow-worker-thread'\n      config:\n        provider: spawn\n\n    - id: tool-workflow\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-workflow'\n\n    - id: tool-ralph\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-ralph'\n      config:\n        subagentProvider: spawn\n        maxRounds: 64\n\n# ── dsh-plans role subagents ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Local module relative to this composition file (the loader resolves `./`\n# against the preset directory). Provides no service — it only registers a\n# tool into this preset's layer and consumes the host `subagents` registry and\n# `llm` model catalog — so it needs no isolate realm.\n#\n# `config.deny` is the child's read-only filter: every named tool is denied\n# to reviewer/criticizer children. Only name tools that exist in this\n# preset's catalog — `tools.restrict` rejects unknown names, and the disabled\n# product-provider rows below the delegation group are NOT in the catalog.\n- id: plan-subagents-tool\n  name: ./lib/plan-subagents.js\n  config:\n    toolName: run_plan_subagent\n    provider: spawn\n    deny:\n      - write\n      - edit\n      - todo_write\n      - create_goal\n      - get_goal\n      - update_goal\n      - ask_user_question\n      - run_plan_subagent\n      - subagent\n      - subagent_fork\n      - send_message\n      - interrupt_agent\n      - list_agents\n      - workflow\n      - ralph\n\n# ── remaining model-facing rows ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n- id: tool-ask-user\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-ask-user'\n\n- id: tool-todo\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-todo'\n  config:\n    allowParallelInProgress: true\n\n# The `web` service and its search provider stay in the host composition; only\n# the model-facing tool is per-session.\n- id: tool-web\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-web'\n  config:\n    fetch: false\n    searchTimeoutMs: 60000\n\n# ── presentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Present every registered tool through the host's generated TypeScript SDK.\n# The official selector waits for the host-plane `codeRuntime` and makes preset\n# mounting fail clearly when that prerequisite is absent; there is no Native\n# fallback because it would restore the Bash schema incompatibility.\n- id: tool-presentation\n  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-tool-presentation'\n  config:\n    mode: code\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "lib/plan-subagents.js",
      "content": "// dsh-plans: model-selectable, read-only planning-role subagent tool.\n//\n// The stock `subagent` tool fixes the child model at composition time, but the\n// dsh-plans workflow persists a per-workspace model choice for each role\n// (reviewer / criticizer) and passes it at spawn time. This small host plugin\n// registers `run_plan_subagent`, which wraps the host `subagents` service with\n// a runtime `model` parameter. It also denies the child the mutation, goal,\n// user-question, and delegation tools, so reviewer/criticizer children are\n// read-only structurally, not just by prompt.\n//\n// The file is plain CommonJS on purpose: the preset directory has no\n// package.json, and the composition loader imports this module relative to the\n// preset's own directory. No imports are used, so no node_modules resolution\n// is needed. The read-only deny list is supplied by the composition's\n// `config.deny` (data, not code), so it can be edited without touching this\n// module and is re-read on every mount.\n\nasync function resolveAgentOptions(llm, selector) {\n  const providers = llm.listProviders()\n  const normalized = selector.toLowerCase()\n  const explicit = providers.find(({ id }) => normalized.startsWith(`${id.toLowerCase()}/`))\n  if (explicit) {\n    const model = selector.slice(explicit.id.length + 1)\n    if (model === '') throw new Error('the provider/model selector is missing its model id')\n    return { provider: explicit.id, model }\n  }\n\n  const catalogs = await Promise.all(providers.map(async ({ id }) => {\n    try {\n      return (await llm.listModels(id)).map((model) => ({ provider: id, model }))\n    } catch {\n      return []\n    }\n  }))\n  const matches = catalogs.flat().filter(({ model }) =>\n    model.id.toLowerCase() === normalized ||\n    (typeof model.name === 'string' && model.name.toLowerCase() === normalized)\n  )\n\n  if (matches.length === 1) return { provider: matches[0].provider, model: matches[0].model.id }\n  if (matches.length === 0) throw new Error('selector was not found in the current model catalog; use a model row label or provider/model id')\n  throw new Error(`selector is ambiguous; use one of: ${matches.map(({ provider, model }) => `${provider}/${model.id}`).join(', ')}`)\n}\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  name: 'dsh-plans-plan-subagents',\n\n  inject: ['tools', 'subagents', 'llm'],\n\n  apply(ctx, config) {\n    const toolName = typeof config.toolName === 'string' && config.toolName !== '' ? config.toolName : 'run_plan_subagent'\n    const provider = typeof config.provider === 'string' && config.provider !== '' ? config.provider : 'spawn'\n    const deny = Array.isArray(config.deny) ? config.deny.filter((name) => typeof name === 'string') : []\n\n    const definition = {\n      name: toolName,\n      description: 'Delegate one planning-role pass (reviewer or criticizer) to a fresh subagent that works in its own context and returns its final report. Use it only for dsh-plans reviewer/criticizer rounds after the user answered the refinement mode question. The child is read-only by construction: file-write tools, goal tools, user questions, and delegation tools are denied to it. It runs in the foreground: the call returns the child\\'s complete final report. The optional model parameter is the persisted model ID or display name from dsh-plans/.state/config.json for the role; omit it to inherit the current session model.',\n      parameters: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          description: {\n            type: 'string',\n            description: 'A short (3-5 word) label of the delegated role pass, e.g. \"reviewer round 1\" or \"<topic>-review-a\".',\n          },\n          prompt: {\n            type: 'string',\n            description: 'The complete, self-contained brief for the subagent. It does not share this conversation\\'s context, so include everything it needs: the absolute path of the PLAN_vN.md to review, the read-only instruction, the artifact directory (it must NOT write files), and the required findings report format.',\n          },\n          model: {\n            type: 'string',\n            description: 'Optional model ID, display name, or provider/model ID persisted for this role. It is resolved against the current DSH model catalog. Omit it to inherit the current session model. Pass only what the user confirmed.',\n          },\n        },\n        required: ['description', 'prompt'],\n      },\n      output: {\n        schema: { type: 'string' },\n        render(_args, value) {\n          return [{ type: 'text', text: value }]\n        },\n      },\n      async execute(args, exec) {\n        const parent = exec.agent\n        if (!parent) throw new Error('run_plan_subagent requires a calling agent (exec.agent was undefined)')\n\n        const request = {\n          label: String(args.description ?? ''),\n          prompt: [{ type: 'text', text: String(args.prompt ?? '') }],\n          parent,\n          toolFilter: { deny },\n        }\n        const modelSelector = typeof args.model === 'string' && args.model.trim() !== '' ? args.model.trim() : undefined\n        if (modelSelector !== undefined) {\n          try {\n            request.agentOptions = await resolveAgentOptions(ctx.llm, modelSelector)\n          } catch (error) {\n            throw new Error(`run_plan_subagent could not resolve model \"${modelSelector}\": ${String(error && error.message ? error.message : error)}`)\n          }\n        }\n\n        let run\n        try {\n          run = await ctx.subagents.start(provider, { ...request, signal: exec.signal })\n        } catch (error) {\n          throw new Error(\n            `run_plan_subagent could not start${modelSelector ? ` with model \"${modelSelector}\"` : ''}: ${String(error && error.message ? error.message : error)}`\n          )\n        }\n\n        const [execution] = await Promise.allSettled([run.result])\n        const [disposal] = await Promise.allSettled([Promise.resolve().then(() => run.dispose())])\n\n        if (execution.status === 'rejected') {\n          const detail = String(execution.reason && execution.reason.message ? execution.reason.message : execution.reason)\n          if (disposal.status === 'rejected') {\n            throw new Error(`run_plan_subagent run failed: ${detail}; dispose failed: ${String(disposal.reason && disposal.reason.message ? disposal.reason.message : disposal.reason)}`)\n          }\n          throw new Error(`run_plan_subagent run failed: ${detail}`)\n        }\n        if (disposal.status === 'rejected') {\n          throw new Error(`run_plan_subagent dispose failed: ${String(disposal.reason && disposal.reason.message ? disposal.reason.message : disposal.reason)}`)\n        }\n\n        const result = execution.value\n        const text = (Array.isArray(result && result.output) ? result.output : [])\n          .filter((block) => block && typeof block === 'object' && block.type === 'text' && typeof block.text === 'string')\n          .map((block) => block.text)\n          .join('')\n\n        if (result && result.stopReason !== 'completed') {\n          const reason = result.stopReason != null ? String(result.stopReason) : 'unknown'\n          const suffix = text.length > 0 ? ` Partial output before the child ended:\\n${text}` : ''\n          throw new Error(`run_plan_subagent ended abnormally (${reason}) before it finished.${suffix}`)\n        }\n\n        return text\n      },\n    }\n\n    const dispose = ctx.tools.register(definition)\n    return () => dispose()\n  },\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "preset.yml",
      "content": "name: 规划模式（dsh-plans）\ndescription: 人类在环的计划工作流：变更前先产出经过研究、评审与批评子代理打磨的 Markdown 计划（dsh-plans/），经显式交接后作为 DSH goal 执行（ponytail + MVP 最小测试）。每个工作目录首次使用会询问语言与 reviewer/criticizer/executor 模型。具备标准模式的全部能力。\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "scripts/dsh_plans_state.py",
      "content": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Manage dsh-plans workspace state under <workdir>/dsh-plans/.state/.\n\ndsh-plans adapts the prime-plans workflow (https://github.com/Optim-Agent/prime-plans)\nto the DeepSeek Harness. Public planning artifacts live in the committed\n`<workdir>/dsh-plans/` directory; machine state lives beside them in the\nprivate `<workdir>/dsh-plans/.state/` directory, which `init` keeps out of git\nby ensuring `dsh-plans/.gitignore` contains `.state/`. No git repository is\nrequired and none is created: state is simply per working directory.\n\nThe script is standard-library Python and intentionally small; the agent runs\nit through the bash tool. `show` is strictly read-only.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport datetime as dt\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nARTIFACT_DIRNAME = \"dsh-plans\"\nPRIVATE_DIRNAME = \".state\"\nSLUG_RE = re.compile(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\")\n\nDEFAULT_CONFIG: dict[str, Any] = {\n    \"schema\": 1,\n    \"language\": {\n        \"tag\": None,\n        \"source\": \"unset\",\n        \"updated_at\": None,\n    },\n    \"reviewer\": {\n        \"mode\": \"delegated-subagent\",\n        \"model_selector\": None,\n        \"confirmed_at\": None,\n    },\n    \"criticizer\": {\n        \"mode\": \"delegated-subagent\",\n        \"model_selector\": None,\n        \"confirmed_at\": None,\n    },\n    \"executor\": {\n        \"mode\": \"goal-loop\",\n        \"model_selector\": None,\n        \"confirmed_at\": None,\n    },\n    \"artifact_root\": ARTIFACT_DIRNAME,\n}\n\nVALID_ROLES = {\"reviewer\", \"criticizer\", \"executor\"}\nVALID_ROLE_MODES = {\"delegated-subagent\", \"current-session\"}\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    return (\n        dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)\n        .replace(microsecond=0)\n        .isoformat()\n        .replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n    )\n\n\ndef normalize_workdir(value: str) -> Path:\n    return Path(value).expanduser().resolve()\n\n\ndef artifact_root_for(workdir: Path, config: dict[str, Any]) -> Path:\n    root = Path(config.get(\"artifact_root\", ARTIFACT_DIRNAME))\n    return root if root.is_absolute() else workdir / root\n\n\ndef state_root_for(workdir: Path, config: dict[str, Any]) -> Path:\n    return artifact_root_for(workdir, config) / PRIVATE_DIRNAME\n\n\ndef atomic_write_json(path: Path, data: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tmp = path.with_suffix(path.suffix + \".tmp\")\n    tmp.write_text(\n        json.dumps(data, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\"\n    )\n    tmp.replace(path)\n\n\ndef deep_merge_defaults(data: dict[str, Any], defaults: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    merged = dict(data)\n    for key, value in defaults.items():\n        if key not in merged:\n            merged[key] = value\n        elif isinstance(value, dict) and isinstance(merged[key], dict):\n            merged[key] = deep_merge_defaults(merged[key], value)\n    return merged\n\n\ndef load_config(state: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    path = state / \"config.json\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        return json.loads(json.dumps(DEFAULT_CONFIG))\n    data = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    return deep_merge_defaults(data, DEFAULT_CONFIG)\n\n\ndef ensure_gitignored(artifact_root: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Keep `.state/` out of git without touching anything else.\"\"\"\n    ignore = artifact_root / \".gitignore\"\n    entry = PRIVATE_DIRNAME + \"/\"\n    raw = \"\"\n    if ignore.exists():\n        raw = ignore.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        if any(line.strip().rstrip(\"/\") == PRIVATE_DIRNAME for line in raw.splitlines()):\n            return\n    raw_ends_with_newline = raw.endswith(\"\\n\")\n    with ignore.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n        if ignore.exists() and not raw_ends_with_newline:\n            handle.write(\"\\n\")\n        handle.write(f\"# dsh-plans machine state; never commit\\n{entry}\\n\")\n\n\ndef _ensure(workdir: Path) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], Path]:\n    config = load_config(workdir / ARTIFACT_DIRNAME / PRIVATE_DIRNAME)\n    artifact_root = artifact_root_for(workdir, config)\n    state = state_root_for(workdir, config)\n    artifact_root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    state.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for sub in (\"runs\", \"tmp\", \"cache\"):\n        (state / sub).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    ensure_gitignored(artifact_root)\n    atomic_write_json(state / \"config.json\", config)\n    return config, state\n\n\ndef ensure_state(workdir: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return _ensure(workdir)[0]\n\n\ndef show_state(workdir: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    state = workdir / ARTIFACT_DIRNAME / PRIVATE_DIRNAME\n    config_file = state / \"config.json\"\n    if not config_file.is_file():\n        raise SystemExit(\n            \"no dsh-plans state found; run `dsh_plans_state.py init` first\"\n        )\n    return load_config(state)\n\n\ndef set_language(workdir: Path, tag: str, source: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    if source not in {\"user\", \"auto\"}:\n        raise SystemExit(\"--source must be user or auto\")\n    config, state = _ensure(workdir)\n    config[\"language\"] = {\n        \"tag\": tag,\n        \"source\": source,\n        \"updated_at\": utc_now(),\n    }\n    atomic_write_json(state / \"config.json\", config)\n    return config\n\n\ndef set_role(\n    workdir: Path,\n    role: str,\n    mode: str | None,\n    model_selector: str | None,\n    confirmed: bool,\n    reset_confirmation: bool,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    if role not in VALID_ROLES:\n        raise SystemExit(\"--role must be one of \" + \", \".join(sorted(VALID_ROLES)))\n    if mode is not None and role == \"executor\":\n        raise SystemExit(\n            \"--mode is not valid for the executor role; execution always runs as \"\n            \"the DSH goal loop in the current session\"\n        )\n    if mode is not None and mode not in VALID_ROLE_MODES:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"--mode must be one of {sorted(VALID_ROLE_MODES)}\")\n    if confirmed and reset_confirmation:\n        raise SystemExit(\"--confirmed and --reset-confirmation are mutually exclusive\")\n    config, state = _ensure(workdir)\n    role_config = dict(config.get(role, {}))\n    for key, value in DEFAULT_CONFIG[role].items():\n        role_config.setdefault(key, value)\n    if mode is not None:\n        role_config[\"mode\"] = mode\n    if model_selector is not None:\n        role_config[\"model_selector\"] = (\n            None if model_selector == \"inherit\" else model_selector\n        )\n    if confirmed:\n        role_config[\"confirmed_at\"] = utc_now()\n    if reset_confirmation:\n        role_config[\"confirmed_at\"] = None\n    config[role] = role_config\n    atomic_write_json(state / \"config.json\", config)\n    return config\n\n\ndef slugify(topic: str) -> str:\n    slug = SLUG_RE.sub(\"-\", topic.lower()).strip(\"-\")\n    return slug[:80] or \"planning-run\"\n\n\ndef start_run(workdir: Path, topic: str, skill: str, request_text: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    config, state = _ensure(workdir)\n    now = utc_now()\n    stamp = now.replace(\"-\", \"\").replace(\":\", \"\").replace(\"Z\", \"Z\")\n    topic_slug = slugify(topic)\n    base_run_id = f\"{stamp}-{topic_slug}\"\n    run_id = base_run_id\n    suffix = 2\n    while (state / \"runs\" / run_id).exists():\n        run_id = f\"{base_run_id}-{suffix}\"\n        suffix += 1\n    artifact_root = artifact_root_for(workdir, config)\n    date_slug = dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n    artifact_dir = artifact_root / f\"{date_slug}-{topic_slug}\"\n    run_dir = state / \"runs\" / run_id\n    run_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n    artifact_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    run = {\n        \"schema\": 1,\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"skill\": skill,\n        \"topic\": topic_slug,\n        \"request_text\": request_text,\n        \"workdir\": str(workdir),\n        \"artifact_dir\": str(artifact_dir),\n        \"language_tag\": config.get(\"language\", {}).get(\"tag\"),\n        \"status\": \"planning\",\n        \"created_at\": now,\n        \"updated_at\": now,\n    }\n    atomic_write_json(run_dir / \"run.json\", run)\n    for name in (\"decisions.jsonl\", \"subagents.jsonl\", \"refs.jsonl\"):\n        (run_dir / name).touch(exist_ok=True)\n    atomic_write_json(\n        state / \"active.json\",\n        {\"run_id\": run_id, \"run_dir\": str(run_dir), \"artifact_dir\": str(artifact_dir)},\n    )\n    return run\n\n\ndef record_subagent(\n    workdir: Path,\n    run_id: str,\n    role: str,\n    label: str,\n    model: str | None,\n    status: str | None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    if role not in {\"reviewer\", \"criticizer\"}:\n        raise SystemExit(\"--role must be reviewer or criticizer\")\n    _, state = _ensure(workdir)\n    path = state / \"runs\" / run_id / \"subagents.jsonl\"\n    if not path.parent.is_dir():\n        raise SystemExit(f\"run does not exist: {run_id}\")\n    entry = {\n        \"role\": role,\n        \"label\": label,\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"status\": status,\n        \"recorded_at\": utc_now(),\n    }\n    with path.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n        handle.write(json.dumps(entry, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")\n    return entry\n\n\ndef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Manage dsh-plans workspace state for the DeepSeek Harness: \"\n        \"planning artifacts in dsh-plans/, machine state in dsh-plans/.state/\"\n    )\n    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n\n    init = sub.add_parser(\"init\", help=\"ensure artifact dir + state under <workdir>/dsh-plans/.state\")\n    init.add_argument(\"--workdir\", default=\".\")\n\n    show = sub.add_parser(\"show\", help=\"print config JSON (read-only; never creates state)\")\n    show.add_argument(\"--workdir\", default=\".\")\n\n    language = sub.add_parser(\"set-language\", help=\"persist language setting\")\n    language.add_argument(\"--workdir\", default=\".\")\n    language.add_argument(\"--tag\", required=True)\n    language.add_argument(\"--source\", choices=[\"user\", \"auto\"], required=True)\n\n    role = sub.add_parser(\n        \"set-role\", help=\"persist reviewer, criticizer, or executor setting \"\n        \"(omitted flags keep stored values)\"\n    )\n    role.add_argument(\"--workdir\", default=\".\")\n    role.add_argument(\"--role\", choices=sorted(VALID_ROLES), required=True)\n    role.add_argument(\n        \"--mode\",\n        choices=sorted(VALID_ROLE_MODES),\n        help=\"reviewer/criticizer only; the executor mode is always goal-loop\",\n    )\n    role.add_argument(\n        \"--model-selector\",\n        help=\"exact model selector, or 'inherit' to reset to the inherited session model\",\n    )\n    role.add_argument(\n        \"--confirmed\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"stamp confirmed_at=now (used by the confirmation flow)\"\n    )\n    role.add_argument(\n        \"--reset-confirmation\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"clear confirmed_at (re-triggers the first-use question)\"\n    )\n\n    run = sub.add_parser(\"start-run\", help=\"create run state and artifact directory\")\n    run.add_argument(\"--workdir\", default=\".\")\n    run.add_argument(\"--topic\", required=True)\n    run.add_argument(\"--skill\", required=True)\n    run.add_argument(\"--request-text\", required=True)\n\n    subagent = sub.add_parser(\"record-subagent\", help=\"append a reviewer or criticizer child record\")\n    subagent.add_argument(\"--workdir\", default=\".\")\n    subagent.add_argument(\"--run-id\", required=True)\n    subagent.add_argument(\"--role\", choices=[\"reviewer\", \"criticizer\"], required=True)\n    subagent.add_argument(\"--label\", required=True)\n    subagent.add_argument(\"--model\", help=\"exact selector, or 'inherit'\")\n    subagent.add_argument(\"--status\", help=\"e.g. completed, failed, skipped\")\n\n    return parser\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    args = build_parser().parse_args()\n    workdir = normalize_workdir(args.workdir)\n    if args.command == \"init\":\n        result = ensure_state(workdir)\n    elif args.command == \"show\":\n        result = show_state(workdir)\n    elif args.command == \"set-language\":\n        result = set_language(workdir, args.tag, args.source)\n    elif args.command == \"set-role\":\n        result = set_role(\n            workdir, args.role, args.mode, args.model_selector, args.confirmed, args.reset_confirmation\n        )\n    elif args.command == \"start-run\":\n        result = start_run(workdir, args.topic, args.skill, args.request_text)\n    elif args.command == \"record-subagent\":\n        result = record_subagent(workdir, args.run_id, args.role, args.label, args.model, args.status)\n    else:\n        raise AssertionError(args.command)\n    print(json.dumps(result, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n"
